  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342121",
      "title": "Configuring TypeScript",
      "lectureOrder": 499,
      "videoOrder": 441,
      "sourceHash": "4448e15b044d41f48f9842c3488eb406bcf04d2ce15c6068a4f74f0d0b13500a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.26,
          "end": 3.79,
          "en": "Now, I will not dive into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.79,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "all possible types we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 8.8,
          "en": "Instead I wanna focus on a couple of core features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.8,
          "end": 10.7,
          "en": "Therefore, as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.7,
          "end": 13.76,
          "en": "let's add some configuration to this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.76,
          "end": 15.31,
          "en": "So that they can briefly walk you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.31,
          "end": 16.61,
          "en": "through some Core Settings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.61,
          "end": 18.6,
          "en": "especially one Core Setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 20.59,
          "en": "We can add a Configuration file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.59,
          "end": 22.81,
          "en": "which will then be taken into account by the TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 22.81,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "compiler to this project by running tsc--init.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 30.445,
          "en": "This adds a tsconfig.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.445,
          "end": 34.07,
          "en": "which has quite a lot of options you can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.07,
          "end": 37.75,
          "en": "Now, you can read through these comments here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.75,
          "end": 40.36,
          "en": "I do talk about the options in greater detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.36,
          "end": 43.49,
          "en": "In my Understanding TypeScript Course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.49,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "Here, I will leave most options as they are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 49.53,
          "en": "so I will not comment them in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 52.91,
          "en": "but I wanna talk about this \"Strict\" option because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.91,
          "end": 54.117,
          "en": "that is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.117,
          "end": 57.2,
          "en": "\"Strict\" mode is generally encouraged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.2,
          "end": 59.83,
          "en": "It means that certain things are not allowed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.83,
          "end": 62.71,
          "en": "which normally would be allowed in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.71,
          "end": 64.91,
          "en": "And we see this in app.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.91,
          "end": 66.53,
          "en": "just by adding this configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.53,
          "end": 70.58,
          "en": "I now get an error here that this is possibly 'null'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.58,
          "end": 73.46000000000001,
          "en": "This is one \"strict\" mode feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.46000000000001,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "We have this \"strictNullCheck\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "which is turned on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 79.76,
          "en": "All those checks here are turned on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.76,
          "end": 81.35,
          "en": "If \"strict\" is set to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.35,
          "end": 84.11,
          "en": "alternatively, you comment out to this line and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.11,
          "end": 87.7,
          "en": "just comment in the features you want down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.7,
          "end": 91.01,
          "en": "So, they're all set to true when setting \"Strict\" to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.01,
          "end": 93.91,
          "en": "And one of these features ensures that you're not calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.91,
          "end": 97.72,
          "en": "something on something else, which might be \"null\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.72,
          "end": 99.8,
          "en": "And here indeed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.8,
          "end": 101.25999999999999,
          "en": "we select the 'button',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.25999999999999,
          "end": 103.27000000000001,
          "en": "but of course, TypeScript can't know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.27000000000001,
          "end": 105.63,
          "en": "whether that 'button' actually exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.63,
          "end": 109.21000000000001,
          "en": "it does not check our HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.21000000000001,
          "end": 110.85,
          "en": "So therefore this could be 'null'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 110.85,
          "end": 112.12,
          "en": "if we don't find a 'button',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 112.12,
          "end": 113.52000000000001,
          "en": "if we have no buttonElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 114.55,
          "end": 117.57,
          "en": "Now to work around this, we have two options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 120.92,
          "en": "We can add some code here where we check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 120.92,
          "end": 125.92,
          "en": "If buttonElement is Truthy and move that code into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.17,
          "end": 127.34,
          "en": "that if check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 127.34,
          "end": 130.3,
          "en": "Now we know that if this code runs buttonElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.3,
          "end": 132.23,
          "en": "can't be null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.23,
          "end": 133.69,
          "en": "Because if it would be null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 133.69,
          "end": 135.73,
          "en": "it would be falsy and we wouldn't make it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 135.73,
          "end": 136.803,
          "en": "into this if check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 137.8,
          "end": 142.09,
          "en": "Alternatively, we know that there will be a button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 142.09,
          "end": 144.7,
          "en": "Just as we know that these elements here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 144.7,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "are HTMLInputElements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 151.173,
          "en": "In such cases, we can add an exclamation mark here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.05,
          "end": 155.03,
          "en": "This simply means the statement in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.03,
          "end": 156.78,
          "en": "The expression in front of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 158.38,
          "en": "could theoretically be 'null',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 158.38,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "but we know that it isn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 163.53,
          "en": "So, please TypeScript ignored that 'null' case and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 164.91,
          "en": "take the other value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.91,
          "end": 169.91,
          "en": "in this case, take HTMLButtonElement as the only value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 170.17000000000002,
          "end": 171.74,
          "en": "This is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 171.74,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "And that's something I wanted to show you here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 175.47,
          "end": 178.43,
          "en": "One other thing that wouldn't be allowed with Strict mode is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 178.43,
          "end": 182.25,
          "en": "that you omit the type of one parameter for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 182.25,
          "end": 185.56,
          "en": "now it complains that this parameter implicitly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 185.56,
          "end": 187.34,
          "en": "has the 'any' the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 187.34,
          "end": 190.21,
          "en": "There is an 'any' type which you cannot sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 190.21,
          "end": 191.9,
          "en": "and that's also is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.9,
          "end": 194.37,
          "en": "But that's a very generic fallback type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 194.37,
          "end": 197.52,
          "en": "It basically carries no extra type information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.52,
          "end": 200.26,
          "en": "Any kind of value is allowed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.26,
          "end": 202.81,
          "en": "And therefore, this is really just a type you should know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.81,
          "end": 206.32999999999998,
          "en": "If you have no idea, which kind of data you can expect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 206.32999999999998,
          "end": 207.84,
          "en": "if you do know it better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "it is recommended that you are as clear as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 214.73,
          "en": "in this case that you simply define that you want a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 214.73,
          "end": 216.31,
          "en": "But even if you don't know it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 216.31,
          "end": 218.8,
          "en": "if you set this to any it's okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 218.8,
          "end": 220.82999999999998,
          "en": "But not setting 'any' type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 220.82999999999998,
          "end": 223.45,
          "en": "that's not something the \"Strict\" mode allows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 223.45,
          "end": 225.79,
          "en": "Because then does this implicitly 'any',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.79,
          "end": 228.8,
          "en": "but it looks like you simply forgot to look into this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 228.8,
          "end": 232.25,
          "en": "argument and you should at least explicitly set 'any' to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 232.25,
          "end": 234.62,
          "en": "make it very clear that you don't know better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 234.62,
          "end": 238.3,
          "en": "or that you indeed want to allow any kind of value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 238.3,
          "end": 241.69,
          "en": "So, explicit 'any' is allowed implicit 'any' isn't,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 241.69,
          "end": 242.72,
          "en": "and it's even better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 242.72,
          "end": 246.43,
          "en": "if you set the specific type you are expecting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 246.43,
          "end": 247.53,
          "en": "now important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 247.53,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "As soon as you added that tsconfig.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "Once you run the types of compiler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 255.36,
          "en": "you can still select the file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 255.36,
          "end": 257.113,
          "en": "but then the tsconfig.json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 257.113,
          "end": 260.47,
          "en": "configuration will not be taken into account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 260.47,
          "end": 264.59,
          "en": "Instead, as soon as you do have such a tsconfig.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.59,
          "end": 266.5,
          "en": "just run tsc like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 266.5,
          "end": 270.53,
          "en": "and it will compile all types of files in the folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 270.53,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "whilst taking the Config File into account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "So, only if you don't point at a specific file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 279.95,
          "en": "the configuration file will be taken into account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 279.95,
          "end": 283.84000000000003,
          "en": "And all types of files in the folder will be configured.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 283.84000000000003,
          "end": 286.75,
          "en": "You can still target the file if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 286.75,
          "end": 288.97,
          "en": "Then the configuration file is ignored for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 288.97,
          "end": 290.72,
          "en": "the types of compilation though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 290.72,
          "end": 294.26,
          "en": "The IDE always picks up to config.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 294.26,
          "end": 297.03,
          "en": "So the IDE support is always provided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 297.03,
          "end": 299.023,
          "en": "No matter how you then compile it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
